# ssh_menu config — copy to ~/.ssh_menu.conf and edit for your hosts.
#
# Format:   [* ]Name:user@host:port
#   - Name's FIRST word is the "site" (DEV / QA / PROD here) and drives
#     the colored tag, group color, terminal-tab color, and dashboard URL.
#     Add your own sites by editing the case statements in ssh_menu.sh.
#   - A leading '* ' marks the entry as a favorite (shown first, daily picks).
#   - Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#   - PROD entries require typing YES before connecting.

# ── DEV ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
* DEV web1:deploy@web1.dev.example.com:22
* DEV api:deploy@api.dev.example.com:22
DEV db:deploy@db.dev.example.com:22

# ── QA ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
QA web1:qa@web1.qa.example.com:22
QA api:qa@api.qa.example.com:22
QA db:qa@db.qa.example.com:22

# ── PROD (guarded — asks for YES) ────────────────────────────────────────
* PROD gateway:ops@gateway.prod.example.com:2222
